  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">This Dryad dataset from a Johns Hopkins research team has seen early but measurable use: Datacite records 178 views and 18 downloads. The dataset is also linked to two journal articles as cited-by relationships, indicating that it has already supported related scholarly outputs even though the OpenAlex citation count for the dataset itself is still 0.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The dataset, published in 2023 and associated with work on enhanced mTORC1 signaling and protein synthesis in pathologic alpha-synuclein models of Parkinson\u2019s disease, sits at the intersection of neurodegeneration, proteostasis, and translational cell biology. Its concept profile emphasizes mTORC1 and the PI3K/AKT/mTOR pathway, matching the biological mechanism central to the accompanying research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Usage data suggest that the record is being discovered and consulted, with 178 views and 18 downloads reported by Datacite. While that level of access does not by itself establish downstream impact, it does show that the dataset is circulating beyond deposit. The repository record also identifies Dryad as the hosting platform and shows an additional open instance in OpenAIRE, which broadens accessibility.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">The strongest evidence of scholarly reuse comes from the data-citation links: two publications are registered as citing the dataset. Those links indicate that the dataset has already been incorporated into related research outputs, even though the dataset itself has not yet accrued citations in OpenAlex. The available record therefore points to early scholarly uptake rather than mature citation accumulation.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Other signals are limited or unavailable in the current record. Scite reports no indexed citation statements, and public-discourse data were not available for assessment. Taken together, the evidence supports a cautious reading: this is a biologically focused dataset with modest but real usage and emerging research incorporation, rather than a record with broad documented attention at this stage.</p>",
